{"Race condition in device limit enforcement: CountDevices query and subsequent INSERT run in separate database sessions without transaction protection, allowing concurrent requests to pass the count < limit check and each insert a new device, exceeding the configured limit": 0.8973783850669861, "TagDevice now runs synchronously instead of fire-and-forget in a goroutine, and returns ErrDeviceLimitReached from Authenticate, denying all anonymous access once the limit is hit including for existing devices whose updated_at falls outside the updateDevice BETWEEN range since rowsAffected==0 is treated identically to a new device": 0.9244197010993958, "ProvideAnonDBStore is still registered in Wire dependency injection but its signature changed to require a deviceLimit int64 parameter that Wire cannot auto-provide, and ProvideAnonymousDeviceService no longer accepts anonstore.AnonStore making the wire.Bind have no consumer, breaking wire code generation": 0.7398958802223206, "Cache poisoned on device limit error: local cache key is set before the DB call in tagDeviceUI, so when CreateOrUpdateDevice returns ErrDeviceLimitReached the cache entry persists for 29 minutes, causing subsequent requests from the same device to bypass DB and appear successfully tagged": 0.5775837898254395, "ErrDeviceLimitReached is returned as a plain error which the auth middleware turns into a generic HTTP 401 or login redirect, producing an opaque/incorrect response for a quota/limit condition instead of a clear device limit reached message": 0.88620525598526}